’s primary? See the candidates", "source": "Bradenton Herald", "published": "2026-08-15T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}, {"title": "Kelly Kirschner posts $224K in first quarter, says he's ready to battle Sydney Gruters in CD 16", "source": "Florida Politics", "published": "2026-07-15T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": -5.13, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": 1.0, "poll_sd": 10.43, "poll_weight": 0.19, "fundamentals": {"margin": 0.5, "lean": -6.0, "environment": 7.9, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -1.4}, "rating_margin": -8.89, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.66, "baseline_margin": -3.94, "analyst_adjustment": -1.06, "key_factors": ["R+6 partisan lean in an open seat after Buchanan's retirement", "Gruters' large fundraising and outside-spending edge plus Trump endorsement", "Expert consensus at Likely R and Polymarket pricing near 80% Republican", "Some local GOP defections endorsing Kirschner and one poll showing a tied race"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point Republican: an R+6 district, a well-funded Trump-backed nominee, and most raters calling it Likely R, while markets give the Democrat only about an 18% chance. The single tied poll and Manatee County GOP endorsements of Kirschner suggest modest upside for her, but not enough to move the race out of Likely R.", "watch": "Whether the Republican endorsements of Kirschner translate into sustained crossover support and additional polling showing the race genuinely tied.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Vern Buchanan (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Vern Buchanan's retirement opened this Sarasota-area seat, but the district's R+6 lean still favors Republicans. Sydney Gruters, wife of the RNC chair and backed by Trump, won the GOP primary and holds a large financial advantage, with more than $1.4 million in outside support and over $600,000 on hand. Democrat Kelly Kirschner has raised modestly but gained attention from local Republican groups endorsing her over Gruters.\n\nOne late-August poll showed the race essentially tied, though it is a small, low-weight survey. Expert ratings cluster at Likely R, with a couple of Lean R calls, and prediction markets price the Republican near 80%. The forecast sits at a modest Republican edge with meaningful uncertainty, keeping the race in Likely R rather than Safe R.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.257, "margin": -3.74}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2226, "margin": -5.0}]}